---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 3.3 · Ranged Foundation & Fire Cape" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="3-3" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 3.3</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Ranged Foundation &amp; Fire Cape</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Use the Final Dawn lamp to help reach 62 Ranged for The Curse of Arrav. Then prepare a crossbow and bolts, take two light quest breaks during your Ranged training, and earn a Fire Cape by ranging Jad.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Final Dawn lamp → 62 Ranged → Troll Romance → The Curse of Arrav → crossbow and bolts → Ranged 70 → two-quest break → Ranged 75 → ranged Fight Caves → Fire Cape."
        stats={["62 Ranged for The Curse of Arrav", "75 Ranged recommended for a first Jad attempt; confident players can try earlier", "Use a crossbow you can make; rare weapons and Rigour are optional"]}
        unlocks={["The Curse of Arrav and Zemouregal's Fort", "A Ruff Situation and Crab Quest", "Fire Cape and a remaining enchanted-bolt reserve"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Before starting:</strong> check for at least 60 Ranged before the Final Dawn lamp, 70 Prayer and Defence, Piety, Barrows gloves, Ava's accumulator, 70 Smithing and 61 Fletching after Devious Minds and Final Dawn. The equipment below works without a rune crossbow, black mask, Slayer helmet, Moon/Eclipse armour, Bowfa/crystal, blowpipe, Rigour or Ava's assembler. Keep any of those upgrades you already have, and use Exiles' Slayer, Crafting and Runecraft rewards when preparing for later quests.</div>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Two Ranged goals:</strong> first reach an unboosted <strong>62 for The Curse of Arrav</strong>. After the quest, continue to <strong>75 for your first Jad attempt</strong>. Experienced players can try around 70. If the first attempt feels difficult at 75, training toward 80 is an option before retrying with the same equipment.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Quest preparation · use the Final Dawn lamp</div><h2>Reach 62 Ranged, then help the trolls and Arrav.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i33-ranged-62" number="1" title="Reach 62 Ranged after the Final Dawn lamp">
        <p>If you have not used The Final Dawn's <strong>55,000-XP combat lamp</strong>, put it into <strong>Ranged</strong>. If Ranged is already high enough for a comfortable Fire Cape attempt, choose <strong>Magic</strong> toward the later level-75 quests instead; the lamp rewards one skill. Check your Ranged XP afterward. If you started at exactly level 60 and chose Ranged, <strong>273,742 + 55,000 = 328,742 XP</strong>. Level 62 starts at <strong>333,804 XP</strong>, leaving just <strong>5,062 XP</strong>. Whatever your lamp choice, train from the XP shown in your skill tab.</p>
        <p>For the remaining training, buy a <strong>Dorgeshuun crossbow and bone bolts or bone-bolt packs</strong> from <strong>Nardok's Bone Weapons in the Dorgesh-Kaan mine</strong>. The Lost Tribe, completed in Chapter 2, opened this goblin area; Nardok stocks both the weapon and its cheap ammunition. Bone bolts work with Ava's accumulator. Range a low-defence target such as the <strong>Gemstone Crab</strong> in Varlamore's Tlati Rainforest (follow the caves between its moving nests), Ammonite crabs on Fossil Island, or another convenient crab. Ordinary Ranged-friendly Slayer tasks are a change of scene. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dorgeshuun_crossbow" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Weapon and shop</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Gemstone_Crab" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Gemstone Crab access</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Stop at an unboosted 62 Ranged.</strong> Complete Troll Romance and The Curse of Arrav before the longer 62→70 training sessions.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i33-troll-romance" number="2" title="Complete Troll Romance">
        <p>Speak to <strong>Ug in the south-west room on the middle level of Troll Stronghold</strong>. Troll Stronghold/Death Plateau are already complete. Reach the stronghold via Trollheim Teleport if available, or take climbing boots for the mountain approach; fairy ring <strong>AJR</strong> and the secret door near the Fremennik Slayer Dungeon are another route. Bring <strong>one iron bar, one maple or yew log, rope</strong>, and wax materials: <strong>bucket of wax, cake tin and swamp tar</strong>. To make a bucket of wax if absent, use insect repellent on a beehive, then an empty bucket; combine the materials for the sled as the quest directs. Check the bank before gathering again. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Troll_Romance/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current preparation and route</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Gather any missing materials for the sled" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Cut <strong>one maple log by Seers' Village</strong>, buy <strong>one rope from Ned in Draynor</strong>, and obtain <strong>one iron bar</strong>; if none is banked, mine iron ore at the south-west Varrock mine and smelt until one bar succeeds. Buy the <strong>cake tin from the Culinaromancer's Chest</strong> in Lumbridge Castle's basement. Collect <strong>one swamp tar</strong> from Lumbridge Swamp.</p>
          <p>For the <strong>bucket of wax</strong>, take insect repellent from the house <strong>north of Catherby bank</strong>, use it on a beehive west of Catherby, then use an empty bucket on the hive. Keep the wax for the sled. If climbing boots were discarded, buy ordinary climbing boots from <strong>Tenzing south of Troll Stronghold</strong>; his basic pair is sufficient. For Arrg, make missing Prayer supplies using the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>potion recovery route</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>The quest visits Burthorpe, Trollweiss Mountain and the stronghold again; pack travel, food, Prayer restores and ordinary combat gear, but bank between phases. For the <strong>Arrg</strong> fight, be ready <em>before</em> starting the dialogue: he attacks with melee and Ranged and can hit hard. Use your existing defensive gear, protection prayer and food, keep health high, and teleport rather than risking an empty-supply finish. This quest fight is not a safe death. Claim <strong>8,000 Agility and 4,000 Strength XP</strong>. Troll Romance is the direct prerequisite for Arrav.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i33-arrav" number="3" title="Complete The Curse of Arrav; leave the zombie drops optional">
        <p><strong>Requirements:</strong> unboosted <strong>64 Mining, 62 Ranged, 62 Thieving, 61 Agility, 58 Strength and 37 Slayer</strong>, plus <strong>Defender of Varrock and Troll Romance</strong>. With the training and quests above, you are ready to start. Speak to <strong>Elias White at the Uzer Oasis</strong>, reachable from fairy ring <strong>DLQ</strong>. Use the Old School quest guide: RuneScape 3's version has a different item list. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Curse_of_Arrav/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current OSRS item and phase guide</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Replace the consumed ring before the tomb" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>The ring of life is a <strong>quest ingredient</strong>, so set aside a finished ring rather than wearing your only emergency escape and assuming it will remain available. At a furnace, use <strong>one gold bar, one cut diamond and a ring mould</strong> to make a diamond ring (43 Crafting), then cast <strong>Lvl-4 Enchant with one cosmic and ten earth runes</strong> on the standard spellbook. Dommik sells the mould; mine and smelt one gold ore from Al Kharid if the bar is missing, and use <strong>Shilo Village gem rocks</strong> until the missing diamond is banked. This diamond is separate from the later bolt-tip stock.</p>
          <p>Buy the runes from Baba Yaga on Lunar Isle or an appropriate unlocked rune shop. The <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-1/#i31-path`}>Path of Glouphrie grapple recovery</a> supplies the complete mithril-bolt, rope and crossbow chain if that reusable kit has gone missing. Buy insulated boots from a Slayer equipment shop before the electric sewer.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Bring these items for each phase:</strong> three dwellberries and a <strong>ring of life</strong> (consumed by the tomb jar); any pickaxe for the Trollweiss rubble; then <strong>any crossbow, a mith grapple and insulated boots</strong> for the base's fire traps and electric sewer. A Dorgeshuun crossbow works for the grapple phase. Check the bank first. For missing dwellberries, buy three from <strong>Funch's Fine Groceries in the Grand Tree</strong> or pick them inside McGrubor's Wood west of Seers' Village through its back entrance. If the ring is missing, make a ring of life by enchanting a diamond ring with level-57 Lvl-4 Enchant; buy insulated boots from a Slayer equipment shop. To make a mith grapple, use a <strong>mith grapple tip</strong> smithed from a mithril bar at 59 Smithing, attached to a mithril bolt and finished with rope at 59 Fletching—both levels are already cleared. Bring food, Prayer restores, emergency teleport, a low-weight travel setup and spare inventory slots. Bank/regear between the Uzer tomb, Trollweiss and Digsite base instead of carrying everything at once.</p>
        <p><strong>Combat and traversal:</strong> move away when the tomb's golem begins its multi-hit ground attack; Protect from Melee while passing ice trolls; mine the blocked Trollweiss tunnels; wear insulated boots in the sewer and grapple over the fire traps. For the final <strong>Arrav</strong> fight, Protect from Melee for ordinary hits, move to his side/behind his directional axe swing, and stay out of the venom trails left by small zombie adds. A banked Ranged or Magic weapon can clear those adds; the later Fight Cave crossbow is not a prerequisite for this quest. Claim <strong>40,000 XP each in Mining, Thieving and Agility</strong> and <strong>Zemouregal's Fort access</strong>. A zombie axe or helmet is an optional upgrade; you can leave Armoured Zombies for another time.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Ranged equipment · crossbow and bolts</div><h2>Use your banked supplies before making more.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i33-ranged-kit" number="4" title="Prepare a crossbow and bolts for the Fight Caves">
        <p><strong>Start with your bank:</strong> count plain adamant bolts, ruby bolts (e), diamond bolts (e), adamant bars, cut/uncut rubies and diamonds, and check for a rune crossbow. Aim for about <strong>1,200 plain adamant bolts</strong> for ordinary Fight Cave waves and retries, <strong>250 diamond bolts (e)</strong> for Jad, other high-defence targets and later quests, and <strong>300 ruby bolts (e)</strong> mainly for later high-HP bosses such as Galvek and quest Vorkath. These amounts give you spare ammunition; replace what you use after attempts. Use <strong>diamond bolts (e)</strong> for the accuracy switch at Jad and keep the ruby bolts for later bosses. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/TzHaar_Fight_Cave/Strategies" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Fight Cave supply guidance</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Enchantment_spells" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Bolt effects</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Choose your crossbow:</strong> use a rune crossbow (RCB) if you already have one. Otherwise buy <strong>adamantite limbs from the Keldagrim crossbow stall</strong>; cut one mahogany log from the <strong>Prifddinas hardwood trees</strong> if needed, then knife it into a <strong>mahogany stock</strong>, attach the limbs with a hammer, and add a <strong>crossbow string</strong> at <strong>61 Fletching</strong> for an adamant crossbow. Check for a string first; if missing, use one raw beef on a range and choose <strong>Make sinew</strong>, then spin it at a wheel at 10 Crafting, or spin banked tree roots. Earlier quests brought you to 61+ Fletching. The adamant crossbow has <strong>+78 Ranged accuracy</strong> compared with the RCB's <strong>+90</strong>. In the equipment comparisons used for this guide, that meant about <strong>4–4.6% less damage per second</strong> against Jad, Galvek, quest Vorkath and quest Leviathan; your results depend on your levels and equipment. It is a practical option you can make without waiting for a drop. <strong>Broad bolts require an RCB or better</strong>, so use adamant bolts with the adamant crossbow. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Adamant_crossbow" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Crossbow assembly</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Crossbow_(weapon)" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Weapon/ammo table</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Only if the bank is short: make the remaining bolts" label="Quest preparation">
          <p><strong>Train Smithing or Fletching only if you need to make more bolts.</strong> Making adamant bolt bases needs 73 Smithing, while the later quests need only 72. If you are short of bolts and below 73, train with banked ore/bars or your preferred Smithing method. Then smith one adamant bar into <strong>10 unfinished bolts</strong> at an anvil and feather them at 61 Fletching. Starting with no bolts, 1,200 plain + 250 diamond + 300 ruby needs <strong>1,750 bolts from 175 bars and 1,750 feathers</strong>. Subtract the usable bolts already in your bank before gathering materials. With 70+ Mining, you can mine adamantite ore; use <strong>one adamantite ore plus three coal per bar at the Blast Furnace</strong> (six coal at an ordinary furnace). Buy missing coal from its Ore Seller and fund the coffer for the time needed to smelt your bars. Gerrant's fishing shop in Port Sarim sells feathers. Stop when you have enough bolts for the amounts above.</p>
          <p><strong>Enchanting budget:</strong> each cast enchants ten bolts. Ruby uses <strong>one cosmic, one blood and five fire runes</strong>; diamond uses <strong>one cosmic, two law and ten earth runes</strong>. For the full 300 ruby / 250 diamond example, reserve <strong>55 cosmic, 30 blood, 50 law, 150 fire and 250 earth runes</strong>, subtracting any ready enchanted bolts first. Buy missing runes from Baba Yaga on Lunar Isle or the Wizards' Guild rune shop in Yanille where stocked; you unlocked both shops earlier. After enchanting, check your remaining runes before preparing for later quests.</p>
          <p>If you need to add bolt tips, train to an unboosted <strong>63 Fletching for ruby</strong> and <strong>65 for diamond</strong> as needed, using banked logs, bows or other familiar materials. Chisel a cut ruby or diamond into <strong>12 tips</strong>, attach tips to finished adamant bolts in groups of 10, then use <strong>Enchant Crossbow Bolt</strong> on the standard spellbook: ruby needs 49 Magic, diamond 57 Magic, both already covered. In the zero-stock example, roughly <strong>25 rubies</strong> and <strong>21 diamonds</strong> yield enough tips for 300/250 finished bolts. Check banked enchanted bolts and tips before cutting gems. If the gem bank is short, <strong>Shilo Village gem rocks</strong> are already unlocked: take a pickaxe and chisel, mine and bank the needed rubies/diamonds, and stop when you have enough tips for the missing bolts. The gems you receive vary, so check your totals as you mine. If you have stardust, gem bags are another option. Do not spend these enchanted bolts on low-defence crab training. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Adamant_bolts" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Bolt production</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ruby_bolt_tips" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ruby tips</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Diamond_bolt_tips" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Diamond tips</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Once your crossbow and bolts are ready, continue with Ranged training.</strong> If you already had enough usable ammunition, you can skip the Smithing and Fletching above.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Ranged · first long interval</div><h2>Train in two pieces, with quests between them.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i33-ranged-70" number="5" title="Train 62 → 70 Ranged with cheap ammunition">
        <p>Return to the <strong>Dorgeshuun crossbow + bone-bolt</strong> setup at the Gemstone Crab, Ammonite crabs or another low-defence crab. Gemstone Crab is a low-damage, nearly limitless target but moves between Tlati Rainforest nests about every ten minutes; the cave network takes you to its current location. Ammonite crabs offer an ordinary Fossil Island alternative. Ranged-friendly Slayer assignments can break the routine. Keep the hard-won plain and enchanted adamant bolts for the Fight Caves and later bosses. Stop at an unboosted <strong>70 Ranged</strong>.</p>
        <p>If you are familiar with the Fight Caves, you can try around 70 Ranged. For a first attempt, take the short quest break below, then continue to 75 before Jad.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i33-ruff" number="6" title="Quest break: complete A Ruff Situation">
        <p>This short quest, released <strong>8 September 2026</strong>, needs only <strong>15 Crafting</strong>, long cleared. Speak to <strong>Talia at the Dog Shelter by Ice Mountain</strong> near the Edgeville Monastery. Bring a <strong>needle, thread, one fur and grain</strong> for the stuffed-dog phase, plus ordinary combat gear, a little food and empty space; the small outlaw encounter is not a midgame boss. Follow the shelter, Varrock and puppy trail as the journal directs. The reward opens the <strong>dog/puppy system</strong>; it is needed for the Quest Cape and offers a lighter change of pace between training sessions. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/A_Ruff_Situation" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current quest guide</a> · <a href="https://www.jagex.com/news/old-school-runescape-goes-barking-mad-with-dog-themed-quest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Jagex launch note</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Buy the stuffing materials locally" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Buy <strong>one needle and one thread from Dommik in Al Kharid</strong>, pick <strong>one grain from a Lumbridge wheat field</strong>, and buy <strong>one ordinary fur from Pellem's Fur Store at the Hunter Guild</strong>. This is a fresh fur for the stuffed dog; the ten furs used for Brain Robbery's cats have already been consumed. A costume needle can replace the normal needle/thread if already owned, but no such unlock is assumed.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i33-crab-quest" number="7" title="Quest break: complete Crab Quest">
        <p>Also released <strong>8 September 2026</strong>, this light Sailing quest needs <strong>40 Sailing and 30 Fishing</strong>, both already passed. Take your own boat to <strong>Dognose Island north-west of the Great Conch</strong> and drink the mysterious bottle on the beach. Leave roughly <strong>nine inventory spaces</strong> for the shells; the <strong>big fishing net</strong> used for the island's flotsam can be obtained during the quest. Explore, collect shells, help the crab assemble its instrument and finish the ceremony—no combat kit or supply grind. Claim <strong>10,000 Sailing and 3,000 Fishing XP</strong> and the <strong>shell collection</strong>. This completes another Quest Cape requirement and gives you a break from Ranged training. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Crab_Quest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current quest guide</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="The instrument is assembled from island supplies" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Pick up the <strong>big fishing net near the island's flotsam</strong> when that stage begins. Fish the sea-soaked bowstring, battered barrel and other instrument pieces from the flotsam as directed, and collect the shells on the island. These are quest-local items; ordinary bow strings or a banked construction-plank stack are not substitutes. Keep the <strong>nine free inventory spaces</strong> and use the boat you already own.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i33-ranged-75" number="8" title="Resume Ranged training and stop at 75 for Jad">
        <p>Use the same bone-bolt crab sessions or suitable Slayer tasks. <strong>Reach an unboosted 75 Ranged before your first Fight Cave attempt.</strong> This is a recommendation: confident players can try around 70, and if a run at 75 feels uncomfortable, training toward <strong>80</strong> can help before retrying. You can keep using the crossbow and bolts prepared above.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">TzHaar Fight Cave · earn your Fire Cape</div><h2>Fight Jad at range and watch for his two attack styles.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i33-fire-cape" number="9" title="Complete the ranged Fight Caves and obtain the Fire Cape">
        <p>Travel down the <strong>Karamja volcano entrance</strong> into <strong>Mor Ul Rek</strong>, then enter the <strong>TzHaar Fight Cave</strong> in its outer city. There are <strong>63 waves</strong> in one long run, ending with TzTok-Jad. Bring your <strong>adamant crossbow</strong> (or an RCB already owned), <strong>Ava's accumulator, green d'hide or better banked Ranged armour, Barrows gloves, a reasonable banked amulet and a shield/off-hand that does not ruin Ranged accuracy</strong>. Use <strong>Eagle Eye</strong> and bring food with <strong>Prayer potions or super restores</strong>. For a first no-brew inventory, roughly <strong>14–17 four-dose Prayer potions or super restores</strong> with the remaining slots mostly high-healing food is a starting layout, not a fixed rule—adjust from actual supply use on the first run. <strong>Count your doses before entering: ordinary restore potions do not restore Prayer.</strong> Use the preparation note below for any missing doses, and restock from the remaining ingredients after each attempt. Pack plain adamant bolts for most waves and switch to <strong>diamond bolts (e)</strong> for Jad and other high-defence moments. Keep most ruby (e) stock for later high-HP quests. A Ranging potion is useful <em>only if already banked</em>; no Herblore detour. The holy wrench is optional; decide whether you would rather use its slot for another Prayer-restoring potion or food. Blood spells can heal from a safespottable enemy <em>if</em> you already have spell access and runes, but the route never requires them. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/TzHaar_Fight_Cave/Strategies" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current waves, spawns and strategy</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Make any missing Prayer potions before entering" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>The 14–17 four-dose starting inventory needs <strong>56–68 Prayer-restoring doses</strong>. Count the doses already in your bank. Each Prayer potion uses <strong>one clean ranarr, one vial of water and one snape grass</strong> and makes three doses. Divide the missing doses by three and round up to find how many potions to make, then combine or decant them into four-dose bottles. Starting with no potions, you would need to make <strong>19–23</strong> for that example.</p>
          <p>Use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>ranarr, snape-grass and vial sources</a> for missing ingredients. You can collect snape grass from ground spawns and obtain herbs from monster drops, or grow any banked ranarr seeds when convenient. Harvests and drops vary, so check what you have before making the potions. Keep ruby bolts (e) for later high-HP quest bosses, and replace the food, ammunition and potions you use before each retry.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <ExpandableNote title="Waves: preserve supplies, control the mixed threats" label="Fight Cave primer">
          <p>Use rocks and corners to isolate melee enemies; a large monster can also body-block another enemy while you range around it. Prayer-draining Tz-Kihs deserve early attention, and the level-180 melee enemies can often be safespotted. Conserve Prayer on easy waves rather than leaving expensive prayers on while nothing can reach you. From <strong>wave 31</strong>, level-360 <strong>Ket-Zeks</strong> make <strong>Protect from Magic</strong> effectively central whenever one is free to attack. Later ranger-plus-mage combinations are the real resource pressure: block the mage, use terrain/body-blocking, and kill or isolate the ranger that threatens through your current prayer. Eat or restore during controlled gaps instead of waiting for a crisis. Do not try to memorize all 63 compositions; use the linked current wave/spawn guide.</p>
          <p><strong>Wave 62</strong> has two Ket-Zeks. Identify the <strong>orange/off-colour</strong> one: Jad will spawn at its location next wave. Before killing the last Ket-Zek, heal, restore Prayer, switch to the Jad bolts, locate a safe standing position and put the prayer tab in view. Start Jad with <strong>Protect from Missiles</strong> while watching his first tell; his Magic tell has an audible cue but the Ranged hit sound arrives too late to be a warning.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <ExpandableNote title="Jad and healers: one action between prayer checks" label="Ranged-only Jad plan">
          <p><strong>Stay outside Jad's melee range throughout.</strong> Attack with your crossbow so you only need to watch for <strong>two protection prayers</strong>: he <strong>slams his front feet down and cracks the ground → Protect from Missiles</strong>; he <strong>rears up with front feet dangling, growls/inhales, then breathes fire → Protect from Magic</strong>. React to the animation before the projectile; the Ranged sound arrives after impact. Keep your eyes on <strong>Jad</strong> between inventory actions.</p>
          <p><strong>One action between prayer checks:</strong> identify an attack, switch/confirm the correct prayer, do <em>one</em> secondary action—tag one healer, drink one potion dose, eat one food or reposition once—then return your eyes to Jad for the next attack. Prayer switching is priority one. Do not chain several healer tags and potion doses while Jad is animating.</p>
          <p>At <strong>150 HP (60% remaining)</strong>, four Yt-HurKot healers appear. Tag them <strong>one at a time</strong> between Jad attacks and draw them far enough away that they stop healing him; keep checking every Jad animation. If a crossbow click might path you dangerously close to Jad, switch the crossbow to <strong>Longrange</strong> while tagging, then keep Jad outside melee reach. Healers are priority two. Do not panic or try to solve four tasks in one tick; if their damage becomes a problem, reposition or deal with them in controlled prayer cycles.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Death/retry rules:</strong> the Fight Caves is safe for ordinary accounts and <strong>solo Hardcore Ironmen</strong>, but <strong>not safe for Hardcore Group Ironman lives</strong>. The <a href="https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/summer-sweep-up---agility--chambers-of-xeric-changes?oldschool=1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">12 August 2026 update</a> removed the old re-entry cooldown, so a failed attempt can restart immediately. First attempts are information: note which mixed waves drained Prayer, where food vanished, whether healer tagging caused panic, and whether Jad's tells were read consistently. Before another run, practise the part that caused trouble, adjust your supplies or train from 75 toward 80 Ranged if you want more damage. Finish the 63rd wave and claim the <strong>Fire Cape</strong>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">3.3 complete · Fire Cape earned</div>
        <h3>Keep your new cape and remaining bolts for the coming bosses.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Quests complete:</strong> Troll Romance, The Curse of Arrav, A Ruff Situation and Crab Quest.</li>
          <li><strong>Ranged:</strong> 75+ if you followed the recommended training target, or a successful earlier attempt if you chose one.</li>
          <li><strong>Equipment and supplies:</strong> Fire Cape, an adamant crossbow or an RCB you already owned, and your remaining plain and enchanted bolts. Check how many are left before later quest bosses.</li>
          <li><strong>Optional upgrades:</strong> RCB, blowpipe, Eclipse/Moon gear, Bowfa/crystal, black mask/Slayer helmet, Ava's assembler and Rigour can wait until you want to pursue them.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </article>
